1
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:51,540
What is this?
It is a Fordson DEXTA from 1964.

2
00:00:51,540 --> 00:00:56,020
-What do you use it for?
I have to compete with it.

3
00:00:56,020 --> 00:01:00,740
I run a tractor race, tractor-speedway and tractor-cross we run in Målilla.

4
00:01:00,740 --> 00:01:03,580
-Tractor-cross?
Yes we drive on a cross track.

5
00:01:03,580 --> 00:01:07,260
-Is it even possible?
It is possible but it is bounce.

6
00:01:07,260 --> 00:01:11,300
-It's no suspension on a tractor?
No suspension at all just the tires that swing.

7
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:19,440
We are completely stuck in the chair without cushioning.

8
00:01:19,440 --> 00:01:23,240
It works but it feels in the body when you have run some race.

9
00:01:23,240 --> 00:01:26,140
-Was there several different branches?

10
00:01:26,140 --> 00:01:31,900
For the most part we run TRAKOR-RACE it is slalom and then we drive between set bales.

11
00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:38,240
We run 5-6 competitions a year starting in June until October.

12
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:44,460
-Is there any competition in the future (going forward)?
Yes it is Hylletofta on September 14th.

13
00:01:44,460 --> 00:01:48,780
That's what we are charging for right now.
May hope the stuff holds.

14
00:01:48,780 --> 00:01:53,300
There has been some problems this year because it tempts pretty hard on the stuff.

15
00:01:53,300 --> 00:02:00,800
It is a completely standard Volvo 850 engine with original crankshes, etc., it is not opened.

16
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:04,840
A little for a single tractor in really but you learn to drive it.

17
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:08,660
How do you get the idea to put a Volvo car engine in a tractor?

18
00:02:08,660 --> 00:02:12,440
Hmmm ... you have too much free time.

19
00:02:12,440 --> 00:02:15,260
-Who have come up with the idea to trim a tractor?

20
00:02:15,260 --> 00:02:19,900
Yes that is a good question ... I think it started with that ...

21
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:01,640
Should you buy it?
Yes I can do that ... so I brought it home.

22
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:05,480
It stood in the workshop for a few years before I built it together.

23
00:03:05,480 --> 00:03:13,100
It was not supposed that I would compete with it but just just a fun thing to build a tractor with a car engine.

24
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:19,960
Then was it a friend outside Sävsjö who asked if I would be on a tractor race?

25
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:22,340
What does that mean?
I said.

26
00:03:22,340 --> 00:03:26,500
Well you drive slalom between bales, etc.
Okay, I can join.

27
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:31,880
I went to the scrap and picked up a cabin arch that I mounted and competed.

28
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:34,300
The first race I was 2a.

29
00:03:34,300 --> 00:03:36,660
It gave added flavor ...

30
00:03:36,660 --> 00:03:43,040
... it just continued and then more people were interested in the municipality.

31
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:45,900
Then we started a team.
Team Hylletofta.

32
00:04:30,880 --> 00:04:33,500
Fordson is an English tractor.

33
00:04:33,500 --> 00:04:40,480
It came in the early 1960s, perhaps even in the late 50's around 1958-59.

34
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:44,080
I don't have 100% control over history.

35
00:04:44,080 --> 00:04:48,600
This particular model has learned a lot because I have screwed a lot with it.

36
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:52,900
This engine has a little more horses than DEXTRA has.

37
00:04:52,900 --> 00:04:58,520
Super DEXTRA was a snap better than Dextra you could say.

38
00:04:58,520 --> 00:05:02,680
-What do you use this tractor for?
I have it as a truck.

39
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:08,700
I built a pair of pallet forks together so I can lift all my gearboxes and rear axles.

40
00:05:08,700 --> 00:05:10,980
So it doesn't tempt my back too much.

41
00:05:10,980 --> 00:05:14,880
It is a farm's wear and toss tractor you can say.

42
00:05:14,880 --> 00:05:17,980
The idea is that it will get a refresh.

43
00:05:17,980 --> 00:05:22,860
Now I have bought so many tractors because they break.

44
00:05:22,860 --> 00:05:25,200
It is difficult to get hold of parts.

45
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:31,080
When I drove the rear axle last year, I called five different tractor scraps and there were no stuff.

46
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:36,180
Then I got a little panic because it took me 2 months to get hold of spare parts.

47
00:06:05,380 --> 00:06:10,640
After work, every weekend.
All the free time you had over you on the tractor.

48
00:06:10,640 --> 00:06:15,120
Many friends pushed that now it is soon Målilla you have to finish with the tractor.

49
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:19,460
A week before Målilla we made the first start on the tractor.

50
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:24,200
Then it was 03:44 when it started in the garage.

51
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:30,840
Then my friend Jesper Fager was here and connected the computer because it did not light.

52
00:06:30,840 --> 00:06:34,300
Then we had problems with trigger and get all the settings correctly.

53
00:06:34,300 --> 00:06:38,580
But Jesper said I don't go home first it starts and we were very tired everyone.

54
00:06:38,580 --> 00:06:44,720
People who were here watching went home because it was in the middle of the night, it is really crazy.

55
00:06:44,720 --> 00:06:47,700
I am passionate about what you just want it to work.

56
00:06:47,700 --> 00:06:53,820
When we got the tractor running we were pretty tired so we continued on Monday.

57
00:06:53,820 --> 00:07:01,040
Then when I was out and tested and realized that it leaks oil from crankshaft seal.

58
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:06,920
Then you became quite less and said that you ignore this and can not hold on anymore.

59
00:07:06,920 --> 00:07:10,400
I'll be going to Målilla next year ...

60
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:16,600
... but then the friends came and said we help you remove the engine.

61
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:20,380
Call and ask if you can be free tomorrow.

62
00:07:20,380 --> 00:07:25,300
At 22:45 we rolled the tractor into the workshop and at 00:20 the engine lay on the floor.

63
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:46,580
With the help of Natanael Ceder from Maxxtuning in Vrigstad.

64
00:07:46,580 --> 00:07:49,420
Then it went away to Målilla.

65
00:07:49,420 --> 00:07:54,060
I was thinking about one thing.
The front car when I compare to the original tractor.

66
00:07:54,060 --> 00:07:57,540
This is what the original front car looks like.

67
00:07:57,540 --> 00:07:59,300
This one is a little reinforced.

68
00:07:59,300 --> 00:08:01,940
Because I have built a frame on the tractor.

69
00:08:01,940 --> 00:08:04,560
So I have had to move out the stabilization stages.

70
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:09,160
They sit in the outer holes watch the other tractor so they sit in the interior.

71
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:13,500
I have widened the shoulder.
You can see that there are holes here.

72
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:18,020
I have moved out the shoulder and sanded out of the holes.

73
00:08:18,020 --> 00:08:21,820
So I can angle the spindle joints so I get another camber.

74
00:09:00,280 --> 00:09:05,580
They have had problems that they have gone off therefore I have strengthened on the inside.

75
00:09:05,580 --> 00:09:08,940
So you have welded on a plate on the back.

76
00:09:08,940 --> 00:09:11,040
Why do you have weights on it on the side?

77
00:09:11,040 --> 00:09:14,820
Because the tractor is so short.
It works differently from competition to competition.

78
00:09:14,820 --> 00:09:18,760
This one is very smooth and I easily turn it around.

79
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:25,080
The disadvantage of a short wheelbase is that it wants to bounce and goes very much on the rear wheels.

80
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:27,460
And then you want to get the weight down.

81
00:09:27,460 --> 00:09:31,440
I have made an abdominal plate in 15 mm sheet so it helps.

82
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:36,400
If it is not enough and wants to get the bite into the rear axle.

83
00:09:36,400 --> 00:09:41,760
Then I have put weights here that weigh 40 kg each.
So I have 120 kg on each side.

84
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:44,620
Then I feel that the tractor becomes steady.

85
00:09:44,620 --> 00:09:49,300
Is the protection on the Speedway protection page?

86
00:09:49,300 --> 00:09:53,360
Yes and for tractor cross.
It is when we drive several at the same time.

87
00:09:53,360 --> 00:09:56,860
When we drive slalom we drive on each path.

88
00:09:56,860 --> 00:10:00,380
When it can be close contact, we have these pipes.

89
00:10:00,380 --> 00:10:05,340
That pipe should be along so nothing can come in between.

90
00:10:05,340 --> 00:10:09,060
-How phase you got this puzzle together ...

91
00:10:09,060 --> 00:10:13,880
It was to think about first and foremost to think how long you want the tractor.

92
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:16,300
The engine is based on quite far.

93
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:21,160
I wanted hydraulic coupling so it should be easy to connect.

94
00:10:21,160 --> 00:10:26,680
This holds the gearbox underneath and I have made an adapter.

95
00:10:26,680 --> 00:10:29,480
To get the car engine together with the tractor.

96
00:10:29,480 --> 00:10:36,500
Many times an adapter plate is built on the tractor or against the tractor's explosive cover.

97
00:10:36,500 --> 00:10:40,980
In this case, I chose to cut away so much on the blast cover.

98
00:10:40,980 --> 00:10:44,220
I took the angle grinder and cut it off.

99
00:10:44,220 --> 00:10:49,360
Then I talked to a friend here in Sävsjö who works at a company with a mill.

100
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:53,240
He milled off the cover so I had to measure all dimensions.

101
00:10:53,240 --> 00:10:56,860
I have taken from the dimensions from a Volvo 850 input shaft.

102
00:10:56,860 --> 00:10:59,500
But has the tractor's input shaft.

103
00:10:59,500 --> 00:11:06,660
I drive with a flywheel from rear axle parts and a Sachs 765 pressure plate.

104
00:11:06,660 --> 00:11:12,040
There is no longer the same clutch pedal.
I have taken it from a Volvo tractor.

105
00:11:12,040 --> 00:11:17,060
It becomes like you drive a car.

106
00:11:17,060 --> 00:11:21,280
For original, you switch and brake with the heel.

107
00:11:21,280 --> 00:11:29,480
When driving you can decouple with the whole foot but with the heel.

108
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:33,280
Then it will be tough if you have a hard pressure plate.

109
00:11:33,280 --> 00:11:38,680
So we have the cab.
There we have come to the conclusion that we have to cross the cage.

110
00:11:38,680 --> 00:11:43,280
It is if you overturn so it holds together better.

111
00:11:43,280 --> 00:11:48,680
I have chosen to put pipes here.
So it holds together better in the corner.

112
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:52,640
Have also chosen to tick the rear according to the rules.

113
00:11:52,640 --> 00:11:59,100
I have made double crosses at the back to make it the belt.

114
00:11:59,100 --> 00:12:05,880
The cabin is really just bolted at the screen an iron that goes down into the trumpet.

115
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:10,100
-The trumpet?
That is called the rear axle.

116
00:13:05,260 --> 00:13:08,400
Radial tires are much softer.

117
00:13:08,400 --> 00:13:13,600
I have chosen tires that fit the rim that they become straight.

118
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:18,620
If I swing on the tractor you can see that it is soft tires.

119
00:13:18,620 --> 00:13:21,280
The tractor is not so bumpy anymore.

120
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:25,260
I had some problems when I was driving speedway and it went like a duck kid.

121
00:13:25,260 --> 00:13:31,040
It is probably because it is short.
If it starts to bounce, it continues.

122
00:13:31,040 --> 00:13:35,020
The only thing you can do about it is to stay but you don't ...

123
00:13:35,020 --> 00:13:37,640
... first in goal wins.
Then you can't stop.

124
00:13:37,640 --> 00:13:44,320
Why had you dubbed tires before?
It is so when you ball ideas with others who compete.

125
00:13:44,320 --> 00:13:51,720
Rickard and some others also had ice tires ...

126
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:55,960
Yes, ice tires are probably good so you drive on that idea.

127
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:15,520
The first competition in Målilla I made a giants at the start.

128
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:20,960
When the tractor struck, the rim was flat because the tires are too hard.

129
00:14:20,960 --> 00:14:26,020
So it broke the rims for me so I went home and balled ideas with others.

130
00:14:26,020 --> 00:14:31,560
I cut out a couple of edges that I weld stuck on the inside of the rim.

131
00:14:31,560 --> 00:14:35,360
The rims I have in there are reinforced.

132
00:14:35,360 --> 00:14:42,020
Now I have tried to run original tractor tires and then it can withstand more bumps.

133
00:14:42,020 --> 00:14:45,800
And it gets a little right.

134
00:14:45,800 --> 00:14:49,620
It controls well and I never change tires now.

135
00:14:49,620 --> 00:14:53,960
Before, I was changing all the time but it is hard.

136
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:56,900
-What is this?
Why do you have one?

137
00:14:56,900 --> 00:15:01,460
It is the strength floor that sits there.
It is orbitrol control.

138
00:15:04,760 --> 00:15:07,160
-Hydraulic control?
Do you have to have it?

139
00:15:07,160 --> 00:15:08,880
It is much easier to swing.

140
00:15:08,880 --> 00:15:16,520
If you have completely mechanically as original and you use the steering wheel ball and the nip to you have the kid wrist left ...

141
00:15:16,520 --> 00:15:18,400
Hahaha!!

142
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:22,000
Many people get hurt when it shrugs.

143
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:25,780
Many people have done badly.
-You learn the hard way.

144
00:15:25,780 --> 00:15:29,260
It had become very much steering when driving slalom.

145
00:15:29,260 --> 00:15:31,860
Then they had to be stepped back and forth all the time.

146
00:15:31,860 --> 00:15:35,480
Therefore, I have chosen to build power steering.

147
00:15:35,480 --> 00:15:39,240
Then this is a very special sport ... -Yo thank you!

148
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:43,420
You have to be a little stupid in your head to keep up with this.

149
00:16:08,760 --> 00:16:12,800
Many have agriculture.

150
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:20,140
I grew up in Sävsjö but have also been a lot in Hylletofta because my mother grew up there.

151
00:16:20,140 --> 00:16:22,840
I was very much with Grandma and Grandpa when I was little.

152
00:16:22,840 --> 00:16:28,520
It is well there from I have received it because I work with tractors now.

153
00:16:28,520 --> 00:16:31,760
It is well from where I have been given the interest.

154
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:36,640
The engine is fully visible here.
I we can lift off the hood you will see.

155
00:16:36,640 --> 00:16:41,140
Here I have my little screwdriver that I always have with me.

156
00:16:41,140 --> 00:16:44,060
This must be easier than screwing a car?

157
00:16:44,060 --> 00:16:47,460
It is open so you can access everything smoothly.

158
00:16:47,460 --> 00:16:51,380
The engine I found on Facebook.

159
00:16:51,380 --> 00:16:57,860
It was a loose engine from a Volvo 850 with gearbox and front car.

160
00:17:25,060 --> 00:17:29,500
I have had help building a manifold.
-It looks like a snake.

161
00:17:29,500 --> 00:17:32,460
Yep, it's designed by Jesper Fager.

162
00:17:32,460 --> 00:17:35,320
There are straight pipes on this.
Yep there are straight pipes.

163
00:17:35,320 --> 00:17:38,000
It's screampipe out of the Wastegaten.

164
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:43,380
I have pipes here that go from the cab to the front axle.

165
00:17:43,380 --> 00:17:50,900
It is a reinforcement because I cracked the other tractor so you want it as strongly as possible.

166
00:17:51,360 --> 00:18:00,320
What I have been thinking about updating for next season is the brakes.

167
00:18:00,320 --> 00:18:00,860
It is drum brakes original and that is what we drive with.

168
